  "description": "<p>ML Systems takes homes apart in reverse build order so their materials keep their value. Deconstruction Technicians do that work on site: selective dismantling, salvage handling, and sorting recovered material into tracked streams.</p><h3>Responsibilities</h3><ul><li>Selective dismantling of residential structures in reverse build sequence</li><li>Denailing, grading, and palletizing recovered lumber, fixtures, and finish materials</li><li>Sorting recovered material into its assigned stream and logging condition at the point of recovery</li><li>Operating hand and hydraulic tools safely in an active site environment</li><li>Staging graded material for transport to the resale channel</li></ul><h3>Qualifications</h3><ul><li>No prior construction experience required — we train</li><li>Able to lift 50 lbs repeatedly and work outdoors year-round in New England</li><li>Valid driver's license</li><li>OSHA 10 preferred; we pay for certification if you don't have it</li></ul><h3>Why this role exists</h3><p>Deconstruction is deliberately an entry point. The path runs technician to crew lead to site supervisor, with certification paid along the way.</p>"
